{"step_index":2443,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T22:01:32Z","content":"### 🔍 Root Cause Identified & Resolved\n\n---\n\n### 1. Why the UI Didn't Change Instantly:\n1. **React State Object Identity:** When `LeadsRepository.updateLeadDisposition` updated the lead and called `loadLeadData()`, the web database engine returned the same in-memory object reference. Because React uses reference equality (`newLead === oldLead`), React skipped the visual re-render.\n2. **Database Parameter Alignment:** The recent addition of the `email` field shifted parameter indices in the web SQL runner.\n\n---\n\n### 2. 🛠️ Fixes Applied & Deployed:\n\n1. **Instant Optimistic UI Updates ([`LeadDetailScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/LeadDetailScreen.tsx)):**\n   - Tapping `DNC` immediately switches the state to `do_not_call` with a cloned object reference (`setLead({ ...l })`), forcing React to re-render in `0ms`.\n   - The status badge immediately flips to **`🚫 DNC`** and the action button immediately transforms into the emerald **`🔄 Reinstate`** button.\n\n2. **Prominent DNC Compliance Warning Card:**\n   - When a lead is marked as DNC, a high-contrast red warning box appears right at the top of their profile card:\n     > **🛡️ DO NOT CALL (DNC COMPLIANCE)**  \n     > *This educator has requested not to be called. They have been permanently removed from all active dialing queues.*\n\n3. **1-Tap Reinstatement (`🔄 Reinstate`):**\n   - Tapping **`🔄 Reinstate`** immediately un-flags the educator, restores their status to **`READY TO CALL`**, and returns them to your active Power Dialing queue.\n\n4. **Web Database SQL Synchronization ([`database.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/db/database.ts)):**\n   - Aligned all parameter indices for `UPDATE leads` across email, disposition, notes, and priority tiers.\n\n---\n\n### 🌐 Live Production Deployment\nThe fix is compiled and live on Surge:\n👉 **[https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh](https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh)**"}
{"step_index":2444,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T15:59:13Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\ndon't change the codebase this turn but please verify that the IndexedDB implementation is as robust and production ready as possible.  For example:\nBatching Operations: Never execute single .put() or .add() calls in tight synchronous loops. Group bulk records into single readwrite transaction scopes.  Worker Thread Offloading: Execute all heavy database queries, sorting, and data parsing inside a dedicated WebWorker to preserve UI rendering performance (60+ FPS).Relaxed Durability: Pass { durability: 'relaxed' } when opening Chromium transactions for bulk ingestion to trade immediate disk fsync flushing for substantial write speed improvements.  Persistent Storage Guard: Secure multi-gigabyte datasets from automatic browser eviction by explicitly requesting storage persistence (await navigator.storage.persist()).  Alternative Engine Consideration: If your application requires heavy relational querying, indexing on booleans, or complex joins across multi-gig datasets, evaluate SQLite WASM running over the Origin Private File System (OPFS) instead of raw IndexedDB.  also, whether or not the Dexie.js wrapper would make the implementation more robust and stable.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-08-24T11:59:13-04:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
